---
/*
  Selection as positioning, with the second entry point for the creator who
  lost an account set at the same weight, same size, same spacing.
  04-konzept.md section 4.3, page "/who-we-work-with", and section 3.
  The internal exclusions (professional performers, media contracts) stay off
  this page on purpose. They belong in qualification, not in public copy.
*/
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CtaBlock from '../components/CtaBlock.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Who we work with | Wunder"
  description="Our intake criteria in public, and what we do when you have lost an account before."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>We say no more often than yes.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Here is what we look at, so you can check yourself against it before you spend twenty
        minutes on a call.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Regular reach, not a follower count. What your account did last month matters more than what it collected over three years.</li>
        <li>A confirmed OnlyFans link, live and yours.</li>
        <li>Content in English.</li>
        <li>A visible face. We do not manage an AI persona.</li>
        <li>Reach you did not buy.</li>
        <li>Tax residency in the European Union.</li>
        <li>Time and willingness for the content rhythm we agree on. This is the one we say no over most often.</li>
      </ul>
      <CtaBlock />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>If you have lost an account before.</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        You are not starting from zero. You are rebuilding an account that already worked once, and
        this time you can see every step we take on it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Most people we work with have been through at least one agency, and some of those agencies
        were bad. That is not a disqualification here. The account history matters, the way the
        account was lost matters, and both are things we would rather hear at the start than in
        month three.
      </p>
      <p>
        If your last month was quiet because you stopped posting, say so in the application. It
        changes the plan, not the answer.
      </p>
      <CtaBlock />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Who we do not take on.</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Accounts outside the European Union for tax purposes. We cannot pay them the way we pay everyone else.</li>
        <li>Accounts still under an exclusive contract with another agency or manager, until that contract ends. See <a href="/switching">switching</a>.</li>
        <li>Accounts with bought reach.</li>
        <li>Faceless and AI generated personas.</li>
        <li>Anyone who wants us to run the account without them. There is no version of this where you are not involved.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
